  "comment": "**What it does**\nFinds **solid income REITs** - a fat but sustainable payout.\n- **Pays well** - yield 4-10% (REITs are legally high payers; above ~10% smells\n  like trouble, so capped).\n- **Still growing** - revenue not shrinking (history or forecast).\n- **Debt in check** - leverage within REIT norms, interest comfortably paid;\n  a REIT is never dropped just for missing debt data.\n- **Reliable** - held or raised the dividend in at least 8 of 10 years.\n$1B and bigger, calm-ish movers only.\n\n**How to tweak**\n- More names? Yield floor 3.5, `div_consistency` 70.\n- Safer? `debt_to_ebitda` <= 6 and `interest_coverage` >= 2.5.\n- Bigger only? Raise `market_cap` to $3B.\n\n**How to sort for best picks**\n- **Sort by `income_score`**, tiebreak `quality_score`.\n- **Avoid** `value_score` alone - the cheapest REITs are often cheap for a\n  reason (dying malls, offices); income + quality is the safer lens.",
  "ai_instructions": "Find solid income REITs \u2014 real-estate trusts with a fat but sustainable payout.\nThis fills the type my other screens exclude.\n- **Goal**: income. **Kinds**: REITs only. **Dividends**: required.\n- **Yield**: roughly 4-10% (REITs are legally high payers; above ~10% smells like\n  trouble).\n- **Still growing**: revenue should not be shrinking.\n- **Debt in check**: leverage within normal REIT norms, interest comfortably paid;\n  never drop a REIT just because a debt metric has no data.\n- **Size**: $1B and bigger. **Risk**: moderate. **Results**: ~30-150 names.\n- **Sorting**: income first, tiebreak quality.",
